  "title": "Eth Zurich A Smart Choice For Science And Family",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "To maintain its position as a leading research and academic institution, ETH Zurich endeavours to attract the most highly qualified scientists. In recent years, recruitement has expanded to include international candidates. In fact, the number of non-Swiss professors has significantly increased over the last decade. Today, 34.7% of the ETH Zurich faculty are from abroad.\n\nBut what happens to them once they have arrived? And how have they responded to their new working and living environment in Zurich? By providing a range of integration services, the Office for Faculty Affairs at ETH Zurich makes sure newcoming professors and their families settle in nicely.\n\nThree professors and their families share their transition experience in the following video series:\n\nETH Zurich - a smart choice for science and family\n\nDespite having to make difficult choices, these international families believe relocating to Zurich has been an overall improvement to their professional and private lives."
    }
  ],
